  "script": "In Europe, beavers were reduced to fragmented populations, with combined population numbers being estimated at various locations. Beavers live in freshwater ecosystems such as rivers, streams, lakes and ponds across their natural range. The concept became popular in conservation, and was deployed in a range of contexts to engender support. This approach was mobilized especially where human activities had damaged ecosystems, such as by removing keystone predators. In addition, wolves often kept animals from grazing in riparian areas, maintaining the balance of local wildlife. This protection prevented beavers from having their vital food sources encroached upon by large herbivores. The connectivity of streams to their adjacent floodplain along their entire length plays an important role. Stream restoration or river restoration aims to improve the environmental health of a river or stream.",
